    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 280 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rejection in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): Added an `isCityCapacityReached(...)` check that runs after the city is canonicalized. If the owner's city already contains 8 or more owners, the request is rejected with `400 Bad Request`:\n\n```java\nif (isCityCapacityReached(owner.getCity())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\n```\n\nThe helper counts existing owners in the same city using the same case- and whitespace-insensitive `normalize(...)` matching already used elsewhere in the controller, so differing spellings of a city count toward the same limit.\n\n**Test** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`): Added `createOwnerCityCapacityReached`, which seeds 8 owners in a unique city and asserts a 9th registration for that city returns 400.\n\nThe seed data has only 4 Madison owners, so existing Madison-based success tests remain well under the limit and unaffected.",
